From: rockbandPi
Subject: [PATCH] No SMAA on the highway camera in Low quality

The camera that renders all highways (HighwayCameraRendering) has SMAA set
in the Gameplay scene, and unlike the track cameras (CameraPositioner) it
keeps it in Low quality. SMAA adds three full-screen passes; on the
Raspberry Pi 5 the highway's post-processing cost about 23 ms per frame at
1080p. Turn it off in Low quality, like the track cameras do.
---
diff --git a/Assets/Script/Gameplay/Visuals/HighwayCameraRendering.cs b/Assets/Script/Gameplay/Visuals/HighwayCameraRendering.cs
--- a/Assets/Script/Gameplay/Visuals/HighwayCameraRendering.cs
+++ b/Assets/Script/Gameplay/Visuals/HighwayCameraRendering.cs
@@ -97,6 +97,13 @@
             _gameManager = FindAnyObjectByType<GameManager>();
             _renderCamera = GetComponent<Camera>();
             _fadeCalcPass ??= new FadePass(this);
+
+            // Same as the track cameras (CameraPositioner): no SMAA in Low
+            // quality. SMAA is three extra full-screen passes over the highways
+            if (Application.isPlaying && SettingsManager.Settings.LowQuality.Value)
+            {
+                _renderCamera.GetUniversalAdditionalCameraData().antialiasing = AntialiasingMode.None;
+            }
             _horizontalOffsetPx = 0f;
             _scaleMultiplier = 1f;
 
